# Delivery setup checklist — <% project.name %>

Generated by `/adlc:bootstrap` from `.adlc/config.yaml`. These are the one-time, human-only prerequisites; nothing here is created by an agent. Re-run the scaffold after changing options to refresh this file.

<%#eq options.runner "github-actions"%>## 1. GitHub → `<% github.owner %>/<% github.repo %>` → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions
| Name | Kind | Value |
|---|---|---|
<%#eq options.cloud "azure"%>| `AZURE_CLIENT_ID` | secret | Application (client) ID of the app registration below |
| `AZURE_TENANT_ID` | secret | Directory (tenant) ID |
| `AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID` | secret | Subscription ID |
<%/eq%><%#eq options.base_image "dhi"%>| `DOCKERHUB_TOKEN` | secret | Docker Hub personal access token, or an organization access token (recommended for CI); needed because `dhi.io` requires a login |
| `DOCKERHUB_USERNAME` | variable | Docker Hub username (organization name if using an organization token) |
<%/eq%>
```
gh secret set AZURE_CLIENT_ID -R <% github.owner %>/<% github.repo %>
gh secret set AZURE_TENANT_ID -R <% github.owner %>/<% github.repo %>
gh secret set AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID -R <% github.owner %>/<% github.repo %>
<%#eq options.base_image "dhi"%>gh secret set DOCKERHUB_TOKEN -R <% github.owner %>/<% github.repo %>
gh variable set DOCKERHUB_USERNAME -R <% github.owner %>/<% github.repo %> --body "<docker hub username>"
<%/eq%>```

## 2. GitHub → Settings → Environments
Create `<% github.cd_environment %>` with **Required reviewers** (yourself at least). The CD job runs with `environment: <% github.cd_environment %>`; approval happens before `terraform apply` of `infra/app`.
```
gh api -X PUT repos/<% github.owner %>/<% github.repo %>/environments/<% github.cd_environment %> \
  --input - <<'JSON'
{ "reviewers": [ { "type": "User", "id": <your numeric GitHub user id: gh api user --jq .id> } ] }
JSON
```
<%/eq%>
<%#eq options.cloud "azure"%>> Steps 3–5 are automated by `bash .adlc/setup-azure.sh` (dry run) / `--apply` (idempotent, human-only). The commands below are what it runs.

## 3. Entra ID app registration for CI/CD (OIDC, no client secret)
```
az account set --subscription <subscription id>
APP_ID=$(az ad app create --display-name sp-<% project.name %>-github --query appId -o tsv)
az ad sp create --id "$APP_ID" >/dev/null
APP_OBJ=$(az ad app show --id "$APP_ID" --query id -o tsv)
az ad app federated-credential create --id "$APP_OBJ" --parameters '{
  "name": "github-main", "issuer": "https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com",
  "subject": "repo:<% github.owner %>/<% github.repo %>:ref:refs/heads/<% github.default_branch %>",
  "audiences": ["api://AzureADTokenExchange"] }'
az ad app federated-credential create --id "$APP_OBJ" --parameters '{
  "name": "github-env-<% github.cd_environment %>", "issuer": "https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com",
  "subject": "repo:<% github.owner %>/<% github.repo %>:environment:<% github.cd_environment %>",
  "audiences": ["api://AzureADTokenExchange"] }'
echo "AZURE_CLIENT_ID=$APP_ID  AZURE_TENANT_ID=$(az account show --query tenantId -o tsv)  AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=$(az account show --query id -o tsv)"
```

## 4. Terraform state storage (once; Entra ID auth only, no storage keys)
```
az group create -n <% azure.state.resource_group %> -l <% azure.location %>
az storage account create -n <% azure.state.storage_account %> -g <% azure.state.resource_group %> -l <% azure.location %> \
  --sku Standard_LRS --kind StorageV2 --min-tls-version TLS1_2 --allow-blob-public-access false --allow-shared-key-access false
az storage container create -n <% azure.state.container %> --account-name <% azure.state.storage_account %> --auth-mode login
```

## 5. Resource group and RBAC
```
az group create -n <% azure.resource_group %> -l <% azure.location %>
SUB=$(az account show --query id -o tsv); SP=$(az ad sp show --id "$APP_ID" --query id -o tsv)
# CI/CD service principal: apply infra/app, push images, read/write app-layer state
az role assignment create --assignee-object-id "$SP" --assignee-principal-type ServicePrincipal --role Contributor \
  --scope /subscriptions/$SUB/resourceGroups/<% azure.resource_group %>
az role assignment create --assignee-object-id "$SP" --assignee-principal-type ServicePrincipal --role "Storage Blob Data Contributor" \
  --scope /subscriptions/$SUB/resourceGroups/<% azure.state.resource_group %>/providers/Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/<% azure.state.storage_account %>/blobServices/default/containers/<% azure.state.container %>
# AcrPush on <% azure.acr_name %> is assigned by infra/foundation once the registry exists (output: acr_id).
# You (human): apply infra/foundation, set Key Vault secret values
ME=$(az ad signed-in-user show --query id -o tsv)
az role assignment create --assignee-object-id "$ME" --assignee-principal-type User --role "User Access Administrator" --scope /subscriptions/$SUB/resourceGroups/<% azure.resource_group %>
az role assignment create --assignee-object-id "$ME" --assignee-principal-type User --role "Storage Blob Data Contributor" \
  --scope /subscriptions/$SUB/resourceGroups/<% azure.state.resource_group %>/providers/Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/<% azure.state.storage_account %>
```

## 6. Local shell (for `/adlc:plan` and the human `terraform apply` of `infra/foundation`)
```
az login && az account set --subscription <subscription id>
export ARM_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=$(az account show --query id -o tsv)   # required by the azurerm provider; kept out of the repo on purpose
```
<%/eq%>
## 7. Check
```
gh secret list -R <% github.owner %>/<% github.repo %>; gh variable list -R <% github.owner %>/<% github.repo %>
gh api repos/<% github.owner %>/<% github.repo %>/environments/<% github.cd_environment %> --jq '.protection_rules[].type'
az ad app federated-credential list --id "$APP_OBJ" --query "[].subject" -o tsv
az role assignment list --assignee "$APP_ID" --all --query "[].{role:roleDefinitionName,scope:scope}" -o table
```
Full explanation of every name and role: plugin reference `delivery-knowledge/references/identity-and-secrets.md`.
